  "body": "From the review of PR #141 (#107). `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs:731` calls `ribbon::pinned_set` directly instead of going through a command. Pins are saved in the project file, so pinning a cell is a project change that the history never sees. It can't be undone, and it doesn't mark the document dirty. Pinning on a saved project and then closing gives no prompt, and the pin is lost. This breaks the AGENTS.md law that everything is a command, and it predates #141.\n\nDone means: a pin/unpin command (undoable) replaces the direct write, the document goes dirty after a pin, and both are pinned by a test.",
